course: dictionary
lesson: 8411
title: Runes: old letters and magic symbols
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rune is a letter from an old alphabet, or a mark that people believe has magic or a secret meaning. Context helps you choose which meaning fits. «Vikings wrote with runes, letters of straight lines made for cutting into wood and stone» tells you runes are letters, because the sentence says Vikings wrote with them.
explain: Look at the clues again. «Runes were mostly writing, not magic spells.» The word mostly tells you that writing is the main meaning, and magic is the less common one. In fantasy stories and games, a rune is a glowing symbol with a secret power.
explain: Some phrases use a word in a special way. «To read the runes» is a UK idiom that means to guess what will happen next. It has nothing to do with reading letters. When a phrase does not fit the literal meaning, think about what the whole phrase is trying to say.
fact: A rune is a letter of an old alphabet, used by Vikings and other Germanic peoples.
fact: Runes were carved on wood, stone or bone, often into rune stones.
fact: In fantasy books and games, a rune is a magic symbol with a secret meaning.
fact: «To read the runes» means to guess what will happen, a UK idiom.
fact: Context clues such as «mostly writing» show which meaning of a word is the main one.
exercise: «Vikings wrote with runes, letters of straight lines made for cutting into wood and stone.» What is a rune in this sentence? | A kind of boat | A song | A dragon | *A letter
exercise: In a fantasy game, the hero finds a stone marked with a glowing symbol that holds a secret power. What is the symbol called? | *A rune | A bread roll | A tent peg | A river
exercise: «Ancient runes were carved on the rune stone in the field.» Find and copy the word that tells you runes were cut into something. | *carved | ancient | field | stone
test: Grandad says, «I'll just read the runes and see what the weather brings.» What does read the runes mean here? | To write a long letter | To count the stones on a hill | To carve letters into stone | *To guess what will happen
test: Why is the sentence «runes were mostly writing, not magic spells» helpful? | It shows runes were only used in games | *It shows the main meaning of runes is letters | It shows runes are always magic | It shows runes are a kind of food
exam: Which material is NOT named in the lesson as something runes were carved on? | Bone | Stone | *Glass | Wood
